#34 2.514 
#34 2.515 playwright-cli - run playwright mcp commands from terminal
#34 2.515 
#34 2.515 Usage: playwright-cli <command> [args] [options]
#34 2.515 Usage: playwright-cli -s=<session> <command> [args] [options]
#34 2.515 
#34 2.515 Core:
#34 2.515   open [url]                  open the browser
#34 2.515   attach [name]               attach to a running playwright browser
#34 2.515   close                       close the browser
#34 2.515   detach                      detach from an attached browser
#34 2.515   goto <url>                  navigate to a url
#34 2.515   type <text>                 type text into editable element
#34 2.515   click <target> [button]     perform click on a web page
#34 2.515   dblclick <target> [button]  perform double click on a web page
#34 2.515   fill <target> <text>        fill text into editable element
#34 2.515   drag <startTarget> <endTarget> perform drag and drop between two elements
#34 2.515   drop <target>               drop files or data onto an element
#34 2.515   hover <target>              hover over element on page
#34 2.515   select <target> <val>       select an option in a dropdown
#34 2.515   upload <files...>           upload one or multiple files
#34 2.515   check <target>              check a checkbox or radio button
#34 2.515   uncheck <target>            uncheck a checkbox or radio button
#34 2.515   snapshot [target]           capture page snapshot to obtain element ref
#34 2.515   find [text]                 search the page snapshot for text or a regexp, returning matching nodes with surrounding context (like search snippets)
#34 2.515   eval <func> [target]        evaluate javascript expression on page or element
#34 2.515   dialog-accept [prompt]      accept a dialog
#34 2.515   dialog-dismiss              dismiss a dialog
#34 2.515   resize <w> <h>              resize the browser window
#34 2.515   delete-data                 delete session data
#34 2.515 
#34 2.515 Navigation:
#34 2.515   go-back                     go back to the previous page
#34 2.515   go-forward                  go forward to the next page
#34 2.515   reload                      reload the current page
#34 2.515 
#34 2.515 Keyboard:
#34 2.515   press <key>                 press a key on the keyboard, `a`, `arrowleft`
#34 2.515   keydown <key>               press a key down on the keyboard
#34 2.515   keyup <key>                 press a key up on the keyboard
#34 2.515 
#34 2.515 Mouse:
#34 2.515   mousemove <x> <y>           move mouse to a given position
#34 2.515   mousedown [button]          press mouse down
#34 2.515   mouseup [button]            press mouse up
#34 2.515   mousewheel <dx> <dy>        scroll mouse wheel
#34 2.515 
#34 2.515 Save as:
#34 2.515   screenshot [target]         screenshot of the current page or element
#34 2.515   pdf                         save page as pdf
#34 2.515 
#34 2.515 Tabs:
#34 2.515   tab-list                    list all tabs
#34 2.515   tab-new [url]               create a new tab
#34 2.515   tab-close [index]           close a browser tab
#34 2.515   tab-select <index>          select a browser tab
#34 2.515 
#34 2.515 Storage:
#34 2.515   state-load <filename>       loads browser storage (authentication) state from a file
#34 2.515   state-save [filename]       saves the current storage (authentication) state to a file
#34 2.515   cookie-list                 list all cookies (optionally filtered by domain/path)
#34 2.515   cookie-get <name>           get a specific cookie by name
#34 2.515   cookie-set <name> <value>   set a cookie with optional flags
#34 2.515   cookie-delete <name>        delete a specific cookie
#34 2.515   cookie-clear                clear all cookies
#34 2.515   localstorage-list           list all localstorage key-value pairs
#34 2.515   localstorage-get <key>      get a localstorage item by key
#34 2.515   localstorage-set <key> <value> set a localstorage item
#34 2.515   localstorage-delete <key>   delete a localstorage item
#34 2.515   localstorage-clear          clear all localstorage
#34 2.515   sessionstorage-list         list all sessionstorage key-value pairs
#34 2.515   sessionstorage-get <key>    get a sessionstorage item by key
#34 2.515   sessionstorage-set <key> <value> set a sessionstorage item
#34 2.515   sessionstorage-delete <key> delete a sessionstorage item
#34 2.515   sessionstorage-clear        clear all sessionstorage
#34 2.515 
#34 2.515 Emulation:
#34 2.515   set-color-scheme <scheme>   emulate the light or dark color scheme
#34 2.515   set-reduced-motion <motion> emulate the reduced motion preference
#34 2.515   set-forced-colors <colors>  emulate forced colors mode
#34 2.515   set-contrast <contrast>     emulate the preferred contrast
#34 2.515   set-media <media>           emulate the css media type
#34 2.515   clear-color-scheme          clear color scheme emulation
#34 2.515   clear-reduced-motion        clear reduced motion emulation
#34 2.515   clear-forced-colors         clear forced colors emulation
#34 2.515   clear-contrast              clear preferred contrast emulation
#34 2.515   clear-media                 clear css media type emulation
#34 2.515 
#34 2.515 Network:
#34 2.515   requests                    list all network requests since loading the page. each request is numbered for use with the `request` command.
#34 2.515   request <index>             show full details (headers, body, response) of a single network request by its number from the `requests` command.
#34 2.515   request-headers <index>     print only the request headers for a single network request by its number from the `requests` command.
#34 2.515   request-body <index>        print only the request body for a single network request by its number from the `requests` command.
#34 2.515   response-headers <index>    print only the response headers for a single network request by its number from the `requests` command.
#34 2.515   response-body <index>       print the response body for a single network request by its number from the `requests` command. textual bodies are inlined; binary bodies are saved to a file and the path is printed.
#34 2.515   route <pattern>             mock network requests matching a url pattern
#34 2.515   route-list                  list all active network routes
#34 2.515   unroute [pattern]           remove routes matching a pattern (or all routes)
#34 2.515   network-state-set <state>   set the browser network state to online or offline
#34 2.515 
#34 2.515 DevTools:
#34 2.515   console [min-level]         list console messages
#34 2.515   run-code [code]             run playwright code snippet
#34 2.515   recording-start             start recording user actions
#34 2.515   recording-stop              stop recording user actions and print them as playwright code
#34 2.515   tracing-start               start trace recording
#34 2.515   tracing-stop                stop trace recording
#34 2.515   video-start [filename]      start video recording
#34 2.515   video-stop                  stop video recording
#34 2.515   video-chapter <title>       add a chapter marker to the video recording
#34 2.515   video-show-actions          annotate subsequent cli/mcp actions on the page with a callout that names the action and, when styled, marks the action point and highlights the target element
#34 2.515   video-hide-actions          stop annotating actions performed on the page
#34 2.515   show                        show playwright dashboard
#34 2.515   pause-at <location>         run the test up to a specific location and pause there
#34 2.515   resume                      resume the test execution
#34 2.515   step-over                   step over the next call in the test
#34 2.515   generate-locator <target>   generate a playwright locator for the given element
#34 2.515   highlight [target]          show (or with --hide, remove) a highlight overlay for an element; `--hide` without a target hides all page highlights.
#34 2.515 
#34 2.515 WebMCP:
#34 2.515   webmcp-list                 list the webmcp tools registered by the page
#34 2.515   webmcp-call <name>          call a webmcp tool registered by the page
#34 2.515 
#34 2.515 Install:
#34 2.515   install                     initialize workspace
#34 2.515   install-browser [browser]   install browser
#34 2.515 
#34 2.515 Browser sessions:
#34 2.515   list                        list browser sessions
#34 2.515   close-all                   close all browser sessions
#34 2.515   kill-all                    forcefully kill all browser sessions (for stale/zombie processes)
#34 2.515 
#34 2.515 Global options:
#34 2.515   --help [command]            print help
#34 2.515   --json                      output response as JSON
#34 2.515   --raw                       output only the result value, without status and code
#34 2.515   --version                   print version
